00:19:59,990 --> 00:20:02,550
Speaker 1: It was a commentary of the Old Testament.

256
00:20:03,110 --> 00:20:09,590
Speaker 1: So how come we didn't know all that Paul knew by reading the Old Testament?

257
00:20:09,590 --> 00:20:14,310
Speaker 1: Well, that's where the Spirit of God comes in and the revelation was given to him.

258
00:20:14,790 --> 00:20:15,230
Speaker 1: Come on.

259
00:20:15,230 --> 00:20:15,830
Speaker 1: Is that clear?

260
00:20:16,240 --> 00:20:16,640
Speaker 1: You see?

261
00:20:16,800 --> 00:20:27,120
Speaker 1: So for instance, when you see 120 people speaking in tongues and everybody is gathered around, you know, saying what is going on?

262
00:20:28,080 --> 00:20:33,120
Speaker 1: The Bible says that Peter stood up and said, don't you remember what Joel prophesied?

263
00:20:34,160 --> 00:20:36,560
Speaker 1: This is the fulfillment of Joel's prophecy.

264
00:20:37,200 --> 00:20:37,760
Speaker 1: All right?

265
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:40,880
Speaker 1: So that's how New Testament teaching is done.

266
00:20:41,120 --> 00:20:46,800
Speaker 1: Bringing to light things that were foreordained in the Old Testament that people did not understand.

